      "message": "Our pattern for handling async things like this has been the following:\n\n* You create a mpsc channel and implement an async handler.\n* The topshim dispatcher will send the enum variant via the provided dispatch function. You can forward via tx.send(...)\n* Use the caller id to invoke the callback.\n\nDoes this new async helper provide a benefit over this? Looking through the code, it just looks different (not necessarily better).",
