      "side": 1,
      "message": "This part is trying to establish a pattern of calling btif function that directly accepts a callback, like `BleScannerInterfaceImpl::ScanFilterAdd`. I don\u0027t see there is a pattern like this yet, did I miss it (is there an example I can follow)? \n\nThis makes implementing async abstraction more easily: https://r.android.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Bluetooth/+/2264224/10/system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_gatt.rs#742\n\nwhich in turn makes composing async operations more conveniently, e.g. https://r.android.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Bluetooth/+/2264224/10/system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_gatt.rs#1180 where we can express \"do A until done, and then do B until done, do C until done\" and it\u0027s also possible to compose async operations differently like \"do both A and B together until done and then do C\".",
